---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';

const title = 'Working-group privacy notice';
const description = 'How OPDA uses personal information supplied through its public working-group expression-of-interest form.';
---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  hideSidebar
  hideBreadcrumbs
  hideFooter
  hideComments
  wrapArticle={false}
  suppressActiveDestination
>
  <article class="public-statement" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
    <header class="public-statement__header">
      <p class="public-statement__eyebrow">Privacy notice · Version 2026-08-13</p>
      <h1 id="privacy-title">Working-group expressions of interest</h1>
      <p class="public-statement__lead">
        This notice explains how the Open Property Data Association uses information supplied by
        people who register interest in the Smart Property Data Trust Framework working groups.
      </p>
      <p class="public-statement__meta"><span>Effective 13 August 2026</span></p>
      <span id="contents-title" class="wg-fragment-alias" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </header>

    <div class="public-statement__summary">
      <p>
        We use these details to review your expression of interest and, if accepted, administer
        your participation. Registering does not sign you up to a newsletter, does not give you
        membership or access, and is not used as evidence for AI-assisted modelling.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="public-statement__content" id="controller">
      <h2>Who controls your information</h2>
      <div>
          <p>
            Open Property Data Association Ltd (company number 14789946) is the controller for
            information collected through this expression-of-interest service. Its registered
            office is Tanfield Lea Business Centre, Unit G2, Stanley, Co Durham, DH9 9DB.
            Questions and requests can be sent to
            <a href="mailto:smartdata@openpropdata.org.uk">smartdata@openpropdata.org.uk</a>.
          </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="public-statement__content" id="information">
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <div>
          <p>We collect only the information you enter in the form:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>your full name, email address, organisation, and role or area of expertise;</li>
            <li>the working groups and contribution types you select;</li>
            <li>an optional, length-limited note about relevant experience or perspective;</li>
            <li>your acknowledgement of the registration purpose and this notice; and</li>
            <li>the submission timestamp needed to administer the registration.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Do not include confidential information, evidence, links, property or customer data,
            transaction details, or special-category personal information in the optional note.
          </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="public-statement__content" id="purpose">
      <h2>Why we use it</h2>
      <div>
          <p>OPDA uses the information to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>review interest, experience and potential fit across the selected groups;</li>
            <li>contact you about the groups you selected and, if accepted, administer participation; and</li>
            <li>protect the public form from automated or abusive submissions.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            OPDA relies on its legitimate interests in organising and administering an open,
            evidence-led standards process. You may object to this use or withdraw your interest at
            any time. We do not add you to a general marketing list through this form.
          </p>
          <p>
            Registration data is operational recruitment data. It is not put into the source corpus
            used by AI-assisted ontology or data-model development.
          </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="public-statement__content" id="services">
      <h2>Services and recipients</h2>
      <div>
          <p>Access is limited to authorised people acting for OPDA and the providers needed to run the service:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Amazon Web Services</strong> hosts the form service and encrypted register in the UK region, applies request-rate controls, and carries a reference-only event after a record is stored; submitted form fields are not copied into that event;</li>
            <li><strong>Microsoft Teams and SharePoint</strong> may be used later only if OPDA accepts and invites you.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Registering through the public service does not automatically create a Microsoft guest
            account, grant access or give you standards decision rights.
          </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="public-statement__content" id="transfers">
      <h2>International transfers</h2>
      <div>
          <p>
            Some providers may process personal information outside the UK. OPDA requires providers
            to protect it using applicable UK adequacy arrangements or approved contractual
            safeguards, such as the UK International Data Transfer Agreement or UK Addendum, where
            required.
          </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="public-statement__content" id="retention">
      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <div>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Expressions of interest that are declined, withdrawn or not progressed:</strong> up to six months.</li>
            <li><strong>Accepted participant records:</strong> for the working group's duration plus 12 months.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            We keep information for longer only where a separately documented legal obligation
            requires it.
          </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="public-statement__content" id="choices">
      <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
      <div>
          <p>
            You can ask OPDA to give you access to your information or correct it, withdraw your
            expression of interest, object to processing, or ask us to delete or restrict it where
            applicable. Email
            <a href="mailto:smartdata@openpropdata.org.uk">smartdata@openpropdata.org.uk</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            You can also complain to the UK Information Commissioner's Office. For the association's
            wider activities, see the
            <a href="https://openpropdata.org.uk/privacy-policy/">OPDA general privacy policy</a>.
          </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
